dsv41 patch 0083 (23.10.2026): DSpark depth policy, long-run depth rule. Off by default (lam = 0 = the per-round rule).
Why: the "conf" rule (TensorFold's _choose_k) picks each round's depth by that round's own rate, expected tokens /
round ms. A stream's throughput is the long-run ratio sum(tokens) / sum(ms); its per-round optimum (Dinkelbach) is
d = argmax (1 + S_d) - lam * ms(d) with lam = the stream's rate: a draft row pays when its survival is at least lam
times its marginal cost. In weak rounds (prose) the round's own rate is below the stream's, so the per-round rule
verifies rows with survival ~0.09-0.15 that the stream's rate does not pay for; in strong rounds it is the other way.
What: per request lam = EMA(tokens kept) / EMA(table ms of the verified depth), weight alpha, updated in observe() on
the device (no host sync, the same on both TP ranks); a new request starts at 1 / ms(0). Conf mode only; window cap,
background cap and lookup confidences apply as before. The depth decides only how many drafts can be accepted.
Switches: VLLM_DSV41_DEPTH_LAMBDA=<alpha> (0 = off), depth-file token "lam=<alpha>" (live).
